<DocsLayout title="Lua & LSL Docs">
<div class="dashboard summary-constant">
  <div class="dashboard-header">
    <span class="lua-section"><span class="tag lua-tag">Lua</span><DocsCode code={`NAK: string = 
\x15
`} lang="slua" /></span>
    <span class="lsl-section"><span class="tag lsl-tag">LSL</span><DocsCode code={`string NAK = 
\x15
;`} lang="lsl" /></span>
  </div>

  <div class="dashboard-body">
    <div class="dash-col">
      <p>  <p>The string constant NAK has the value &quot;\n&quot;+llChar(21)+&quot;\n&quot;</p>
  <p>NAK is a value returned by the <a href="https://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/LlGetNotecardLineSync" target="_blank">llGetNotecardLineSync</a> function when the requested notecard data is not available due to the notecard not being in the region notecard cache. The value returned equals the characters with codes &quot;10, 21, 10&quot;, which is to say the ASCII &quot;NAK&quot; character surrounded by two newline characters.</p>
  <p>If the NAK response is encountered, the card can be fetched into the region notecard cache by using the <a href="https://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/LlGetNotecardLine" target="_blank">llGetNotecardLine</a> or <a href="https://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/LlGetNumberOfNotecardLines" target="_blank">llGetNumberOfNotecardLines</a> functions. If the notecard doesn&#39;t exist at all, further llGetNotecardLineSync calls will continue returning NAK.</p>
</p>
    </div>

    <div class="dash-col">
    </div>

    <div class="dash-col">
      <div class="dash-section-title">Tech Specs</div>

      <div class="label-stack">
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
